The core library is LGPL-3.0-or-later. nDPI 6.0 additionally supplies
dual-licensed dissectors, including TLS, QUIC, DNS and DHCP. This project's
default personal/non-profit build initializes nDPI with
NDPI_LICENSE_NOT_FOR_PROFIT_LGPL, enabling those components under the upstream
terms. This default does not grant permission for commercial use of the
dual-licensed components. The unmodified upstream README.license.md is
installed alongside this notice as NDPI-LICENSING.

Commercial downstream builds must select an applicable upstream usage mode
via the backend Makefile's NDPI_LICENSE_TYPE setting. The upstream
NDPI_LICENSE_FOR_PROFIT_LGPL mode disables dual-licensed dissectors;
NDPI_LICENSE_FOR_PROFIT_DUAL_LICENSE requires an agreement with ntop.

nDPI is compiled without changes. The separate zen-appid adapter and its
WeChat hostname refinement are supplied in this repository's appid directory.
The backend Makefile contains the complete source preparation and build steps.
LICENSE.LGPL-3.0 and LICENSE.GPL-3.0 accompany this executable.
